    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1371" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aescŭlĕus</span></b>  (not <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">esc-</span></b> ), a, um,
			adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of
				the Italian oak</i>, and <b>poet.</b>, in
			gen., <i>of oak</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aesculeae capiebat frondis honorem,</span>”
				i. e. <i>an oaken garland</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					1, 449</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">Pall. 1, 9</span></i>.</div>
